{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "07", "m": "09", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "06", "M": "44", "S": "11"}}, "news": [{"title": "Cabinet nod for Greater Noida West metro likely this month", "para": "The Greater Noida West metro project awaits Union Cabinet approval this month.  This crucial step will enable tendering and construction of the new corridor.  The proposed 8.4km elevated line will connect Noida Sector 51 to Greater Noida West.  Five stations will serve residents, easing current commuting challenges significantly.  The project, costing nearly Rs 2,000 crore, is expected to be completed in four years.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/cabinet-nod-for-greater-noida-west-metro-likely-this-month/133863422?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-97824/133863422.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "South Delhi building collapse: MCD seals adjoining building, flags G+4 structure in resettlement colony", "para": "In Satya Niketan, a tragic incident occurred as a five-storey building crumbled, resulting in the deaths of at least three students. Witnesses attribute the disaster to ongoing repair work and excessive water accumulation in the basement. The Municipal Corporation of Delhi has responded by evacuating and securing a neighboring structure. Efforts continue as rescue teams work tirelessly to locate any trapped individuals within the nearly 30-year-old building.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/south-delhi-building-collapse-mcd-seals-adjoining-building-flags-g4-structure-in-resettlement-colony/133862749?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-301620/133862749.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Delhi: Building was being repaired due to waterlogging in basement, say Satya Niketan residents", "para": "A tragic incident unfolded in Satya Niketan as a five-storey building collapsed, trapping several students inside. Locals pointed fingers at inadequate drainage and rampant construction practices for the catastrophe. Accusations of negligence towards building owners and civic agencies surfaced, highlighting public outrage. As rescue teams work tirelessly, the event raises serious questions about safety standards and maintenance protocols in the vicinity.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/delhi-building-was-being-repaired-due-to-waterlogging-in-basement-say-satya-niketan-residents/133862673?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-130240/133862673.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}